he 2-for-1 split trades split-adjusted from Aug 11, 2026. Vendor shares = 1,958.98M (post-split). All per-share calculations use **1,958.98M**. This resolves the SECTION 6/7 discontinuity warning.\n2. **FCF definition:** Filed FY2025 capex $0.132B (PP&E only) vs vendor $0.158B. Both exclude capitalised software. I use filed capex plus a 1.8%-of-revenue forward capex assumption, which effectively covers the gap.\n3. **TTM mismatch:** Pack TTM (through 2026-03-31) shows NI $2.032B; adding the filed Q2-2026 NI ($0.5845B) and removing Q2-2025 ($0.489B) gives $2.128B TTM. Vendor's P/E 43.35 implies $2.16B \u2014 materially consistent. I use $2.128B.\n4. **Vendor market cap cross-check:** $47.79 \u00d7 1,958.98M = $93.62B \u2014 internally consistent. \u2713\n\n---\n\n# SECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\n\n**Step 1-1. Macro Variable Check** (all [Actual] from public data, retrieved 2026-08-24):\n\n| Variable | Level | Direction | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 10Y Treasury | 4.70\u20134.74% | \u2191 +0.44pts YoY | FRED DGS10, 2026-08-21 |\n| Real 10Y yield | ~1.3% (4.70% \u2212 3.4% CPI) | Elevated | [Estimate] |\n| Fed funds | 3.50\u20133.75% | On hold 5 meetings; ~1/3 odds of HIKE priced | Trading Economics, Jul 2026 |\n| DXY | 98.6 | \u2193 \u22120.6%+ from 99.4 in May; breaking lower | Trading Economics, 2026-08-20 |\n| Inflation (CPI YoY) | 3.4% (Jul), down from 3.5% (Jun) | \u2193 slowly, still >2% target | BLS / Trading Economics |\n| IG credit spreads | ~82 bps OAS | Tight / stable | StreetStats, 2026-08-20 |\n| HY spreads | Tight (not fully quantified \u2014 [Unconfirmed]) | Stable | Fidelity profile Jul-2026 |\n| Global liquidity | Neutral-to-tightening | Fed hold + hike risk | \u2014 |\n| Cycle position | Late expansion; inflation above target; labour resilient | \u2014 | [Estimate] |\n\n**Step 1-2. Regime Probability Distribution**\n\n| Regime | Probability | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Goldilocks** (low rates + growth) | 15% | Rates are NOT low; category growth is