vidend or accelerated buyback using the $2.77B cash pile [Assumption].\n\n\u25a0 Risks (downside):\n  \u2022 Valuation compression: 43x\u219230x on unchanged fundamentals = \u221230% price impact.\n  \u2022 Growth fade: international markets mature; category CAGR 8.2% [Estimate] vs market-implied 11%+.\n  \u2022 Competitive escalation: Red Bull (43% share) and Celsius/Pepsi squeeze US shelf space.\n  \u2022 Aluminum tariffs/can costs: management cites \"modest sequential cost increases through 2026\"\n    [Actual transcript].\n  \u2022 Regulatory/litigation: EU or US proposals to restrict energy-drink marketing/ingredients.\n  \u2022 Alcohol segment impairment: $32M/qtr and falling; goodwill write-down possible [Estimate].\n  \u2022 Executive concentration: CEO Hilton Schlosberg and key insiders hold 28.3%; succession risk\n    [Assumption].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\n  Common bear triggers across a portfolio holding MNST:\n  \u2022 Rising US real rates (10Y >5%): hits ALL long-duration assets; MNST's 43x P/E behaves like a\n    25-year bond. Conditional 2-year drawdown: \u221230% to \u221240% [Estimate].\n  \u2022 Dollar strength reversal: a stronger DXY would cut international revenue translation; this is\n    a common trigger across global staples portfolios.\n  \u2022 Recession: MNST historically holds up better than cyclicals (beta 0.52\u20130.70) but a 40x P